WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.738
-As the coronavirus outbreak
spikes for a third time,

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.372
nearing new records
in daily cases,

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.408
the president has decided on
a closing message

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.043
for the last two weeks
of the election --

00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:13.512
whine about having to campaign
in swing states

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:15.915
and attack "60 Minutes"
correspondent Lesley Stahl.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.117
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:22.521
♪♪

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:24.724
Look, I know this might be
a little judgmental,

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.792
but I'm starting to think that,
maybe, just maybe,

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:29.763
Donald Trump is not exactly
a political mastermind.

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:32.065
For example, he basically tried
to make his whole campaign

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.266
about Joe Biden's
record on China.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.600
And then it turned out,

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.903
Trump is the one who has
a secret bank account in China.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:40.206
Soon, we're going to find a
photo of Trump burning down

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:43.542
a Target wearing a shirt that
says "I'm an anarchist!"

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.311
In fairness, if Trump
didn't want "The Times"

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:47.179
to find out about this,
he probably shouldn't have left

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.748
that folder on
his desktop labeled

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.717
"Not a secret Chinese
bank account."

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.885
The account was secret.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.719
Although, knowing Trump,
there's a good chance

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.556
he would have just blurted it
out at some point anyway.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.024
"Mr. President, do you need some
cash for the church service?"

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:00.193
"Yeah, just take it out of

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.429
the secret
Chinese bank account!"

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.631
And then, last night,
Trump was in Erie, Pennsylvania,

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.635
for another one of his
coronavirus infect-a-thons.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:11.237
And his big pitch to voters
in Erie

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.706
was that he didn't want
to be in Erie.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.208
-Four or five months ago,
when we started

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.476
this whole thing --
Because, you know,

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.079
before the plague came in,
I had it made.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.114
I wasn't coming to Erie.

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:25.184
I mean, I have to be honest.
There's no way I was coming.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.185
I didn't have to.

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:27.386
I would have called you
and said,

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:28.454
"Hey, Erie, you know,
if you have a chance,

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:29.455
get out and vote."

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:30.723
We had this thing won.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.792
And then we got hit
with the plague,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:33.993
and I had to go back to work.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.529
"Hello, Erie.
May I please have your vote?"

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.232
-Man, you never hear the crowd
at a Trump rally

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.299
that silent.

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:43.403
"Yeah! We...suck?

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.004
Lock us up?"

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.172
Although, in fairness to Trump,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.441
Erie's not my favorite
Great Lake, either.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.611
There's at least one
that's "superior."

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.881
[ Glass shatters ]

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:59.119
Feel like that should have
come a tick faster.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.922
That joke was originally
submitted for a "Ziggy" cartoon,

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.658
but it was rejected.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.926
Seriously, though, that's quite

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.694
the political masterstroke,
Mr. President --

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:10.797
tell the people
whose votes you're courting

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.498
you didn't want to be there.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.968
"The last time I left Erie,
I prayed I'd never be back,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.070
that I'd never have to look at
your slack-jawed faces,

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.072
and, yet, here I am.

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:21.374
Here I am.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:24.677
Anyway, vote for me,
you bingo-hall townies,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.380
and try not to choke to death
on a sticker."

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:28.914
By the way,
I don't think he was kidding.

00:02:28.914 --> 00:02:30.549
Trump usually goes
for an hour-plus

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.585
at these group therapy sessions,
but he told the crowd

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.720
he was wrapping up early
because it was cold.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.222
-And, in conclusion --
We'll make this

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.323
a little shorter.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.791
You know,
it's like about 40 degrees.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.459
I don't want people --
I don't want to lose anybody.

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:43.362
You got to go vote.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:44.464
So we're going to go
a little shorter,

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.798
because you got to go vote.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.735
-"A little, little shorter."

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.068
Alright, first of all,
how can you be cold?

00:02:50.068 --> 00:02:52.371
Your trench coat could double
as a business poncho.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.140
But, yeah, I'm sure
you wouldn't want anything

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.808
bad to happen to all those
people you invited

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.010
to a packed crowd during
a raging pandemic.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.980
Their health and safety is
definitely your top priority.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.215
You know, we've been saying
this, but Trump is doing so much

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:05.385
to help spread the virus,
he should start traveling

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.920
with a mascot named COVID Larry.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.454
"Give it up for
COVID Larry, folks.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.025
He'll be shooting T-shirts into
the crowd with his T-shirt gun.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.593
We just have the one shirt,
so if you get it,

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.494
put it on, take a picture, and
then hand it to the next guy."

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:16.496
But, in all seriousness,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.830
I'd like to make
this offer to Trump.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:20.833
We will make the COVID Larry
costume for you

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.169
and send it to your campaign
free of charge

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.372
if you decide to adopt him
as your official mascot

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.674
for the last two weeks
of the campaign.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.709
I mean, what the hell?
Just go for it, man.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.044
You've called COVID a
"blessing from God,"

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.277
claimed it made you immune,

00:03:32.277 --> 00:03:34.113
that it made you feel powerful,
like Superman.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.282
You've held packed rallies
without masks or distancing,

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.417
had a White House
super-spreader event,

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:39.652
made people drive
around with you

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.987
while you were
actively infected,

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.989
and told your supporters it's
just like the flu.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.791
I mean, you should just
come out as

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.592
the pro-COVID candidate already.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.327
Might as well give it a shot.
Nothing else is working.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.829
And if you do that,
our wardrobe department

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:52.598
will send you the costume ASAP.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.567
We'll even size it
so it fits Mike Pence perfectly.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:59.339
"Uh, Mr. President,
I cannot breathe in here."

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:00.806
"Just put on the suit, Mike.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.475
Do your [bleep] dance, and let's
get the hell out of Erie."

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:04.677
Every day, it seems we get

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:07.079
more horrific news
about the pandemic.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:09.081
On Tuesday, the CDC said
the pandemic

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:12.318
could cause nearly
300,000 more deaths

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.354
than expected in a typical year.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.122
And a study found that
8 million Americans

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:19.359
went into poverty during
the ensuing economic crash.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.794
Or as the president put it
yesterday on "Fox &amp; Friends"...

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.128
-Well, we are living with it,

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:25.664
and we're having the vaccines
coming out very soon.

00:04:25.664 --> 00:04:27.966
With or without the vaccines,
we're rounding the turn.

00:04:27.966 --> 00:04:30.102
-What's the right path for us,
right now,

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:32.371
on opening up our society?

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.639
-Well, we have to open up

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:36.008
and we live with it
and we open up our schools.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:39.545
And I'm the one that got Big Ten
and Pac-12 football back.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.880
You know, I got that back.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.015
That wasn't coming back,
and I got it back.

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:44.650
Hope people realize that.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.954
That was pure and simple me
or whatever.

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.922
-You really negate the
"pure and simple"

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.857
when you follow it with
"whatever."

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:55.094
"The sky is blue,
pure and simple...or whatever."

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.428
Of course, on "Fox &amp; Friends",

00:04:56.428 --> 00:04:59.399
it's not even a given
that the sky is blue anymore.

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.632
-They went there,
that's where they met,

00:05:00.632 --> 00:05:02.101
and it's pretty much been
green skies ever since.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.402
And, by the way,
they also have the --

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:07.072
-Wait. Green skies?
-Oh, should I say blue skies?

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.275
-Uh-huh.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:12.045
Also, is it just me or does it
sound like Trump's heart

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:13.513
is not really in it anymore?

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.414
You can almost picture him,
on the other end of the phone,

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:18.050
in The White House packing his
things in a cardboard box,

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:21.086
not really paying attention,
halfheartedly making [bleep] up

00:05:21.086 --> 00:05:23.188
because he knows
it's what they want to hear.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:27.026
"Yeah. Yeah, I saved
college football or whatever.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:30.830
Hey, Melania,
where's the insta-pot?

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.933
'Cause I'm
packing the kitchen, Mel.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.302
Mel, you sold it?

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:40.773
With a yard --
Mel, what about my jambalaya?

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:46.678
Mel, what about Tuesday night
jambalaya night?

00:05:46.678 --> 00:05:49.382
Don't slam the door, Mel."

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.716
By the way, scientists
have said we wouldn't need

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:53.586
to lock down again if we just
did a few basic things

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:55.354
that public-health officials
are asking for,

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:58.491
things like testing and tracing
on a massive scale,

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.293
closing down and subsidizing
the most dangerous businesses,

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.796
like indoor bars,
practicing universal

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.299
mask wearing, handwashing,
and social distancing.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.901
If we did those things on
a nationwide scale,

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.336
we could get back to some
semblance of normalcy,

00:06:11.336 --> 00:06:14.540
until vaccines and therapeutics
help us eradicate the disease.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:16.942
Dr. Fauci has said as much,
repeatedly.

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:21.947
-It occurs because of
the lack of implementation of

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:24.951
simple public-health measures.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:29.122
It's so frustrating,
because it's not rocket science.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:32.124
You don't need to lock down.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:33.626
-It's not rocket science,

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.828
unless you're a famous idiot,
like Donald Trump.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.596
Let's remember,
this is the same guy who,

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:40.466
at the start of the pandemic,
went to CDC headquarters

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:41.934
to project
confidence and strength

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.303
and literally just held up
a printout

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.906
of a coronavirus particle
like a 5th grader

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.774
who forgot he had
a science project due.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:52.044
"The coronavirus particle
was first discovered

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:57.449
by the 18th century German
scientist Johann...Wikipedia."

00:06:57.449 --> 00:06:58.951
And, look, I make fun of him
for being dumb,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.352
but I got to give it up.

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:02.587
He is the only person I know
who can get the printer to work.

00:07:02.587 --> 00:07:04.290
The reality is,
Trump and the GOP

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.558
just do not care about
the pandemic.

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:09.461
They don't care that nearly
300,000 more Americans

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:11.530
have died this year
than otherwise would have.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.899
They don't care that 8 million
people fell into poverty

00:07:13.899 --> 00:07:15.601
as a result of
the economic crash.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.570
The one and only thing
they care about

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:21.106
is whining and moaning about
how the media treats them.

00:07:21.106 --> 00:07:23.976
It's the only thing that seems
to get them genuinely animated.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:26.545
They love to complain about not
getting special treatment

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:28.113
on social-media platforms.

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:30.149
My favorite recent example
of this

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:33.252
is a bizarre Instagram post
from Donald Trump Jr.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.387
-Hey, guys.
Hope you're doing well.

00:07:35.387 --> 00:07:38.724
Just watching my algorithms
get crushed.

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:41.594
I guess I did something to
piss off the Instagram gods.

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:44.664
So hopefully you're seeing
this stuff anyway.

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:47.199
We'll do what we can.
Talk to you soon.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:49.368
-I think Instagram might have
shadow-banned you

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.170
for not knowing your angles.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.805
Was this shot from the
point of view of the Teddy bear

00:07:53.805 --> 00:07:56.342
you tell your problems to?

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.811
Also, where are you?
Is that a sleeper car on Amtrak?

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:02.482
And do you have a giant head
or is that a hospital pillow?

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:04.584
Are you going to be Daria
for Halloween?

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:05.885
Seriously, dude,
I never thought I'd say this,

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:08.621
but, you know,
get a journal or something.

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:11.190
Don Jr. is in his 40s,
but he sounds like his best bro

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.259
in junior high
just told him he can't have

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:15.495
that extra ticket to Ozzfest.

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:17.630
"Hey, guys.
Hope you're doing well.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.865
Dirk says he's taking his
girlfriend to Ozzfest.

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:22.968
I guess I did something to
piss off the heavy-metal gods.

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:24.203
Talk to you soon."

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:26.572
This gets to
a core truth of Trumpism.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:28.441
The Trump era has
revealed many things

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:30.075
about what the
modern Conservative movement

00:08:30.075 --> 00:08:31.310
actually stands for,

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.713
rather than what
they pretend to stand for.

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:35.681
And one thing we've learned
over the last four years

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:38.717
is that the so-called party
of personal responsibility

00:08:38.717 --> 00:08:40.986
is actually filled with
whiny, petulant babies

00:08:40.986 --> 00:08:42.655
who fill their diapers whenever
you don't give them

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:43.789
exactly what they want.

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:45.724
It's a party of Veruca Salts.

00:08:45.724 --> 00:08:48.927
For example, last week,
after NBC inexplicably

00:08:48.927 --> 00:08:51.830
did Trump the huge favor
of scheduling a rival town hall

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:55.234
at the exact same time as
Joe Biden's town hall on ABC,

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:56.869
which was scheduled first,

00:08:56.869 --> 00:08:59.839
this is how Fox host
Sean Hannity reacted.

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:03.942
-Moments ago, NBC Fake News
did their best to just ambush

00:09:03.942 --> 00:09:06.746
President Trump
at tonight's town hall.

00:09:06.746 --> 00:09:09.782
He pretty much debated
Savannah Guthrie.

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:12.317
And what we all witnessed
was not journalism.

00:09:12.317 --> 00:09:15.287
It was a political debate
with the morning host

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:18.857
of the "Today" show serving as,
well, Joe Biden's surrogate,

00:09:18.857 --> 00:09:20.792
and it didn't really work out
well for her.

00:09:20.792 --> 00:09:21.961
-It didn't work out
well for her?

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:23.529
I mean, she's still hosting
the "Today" show.

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:25.130
In two weeks, Trump's
going to have a hard time

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.431
getting booked on "Maury."

00:09:26.431 --> 00:09:27.733
"Can you at least
book me on your

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:30.269 line:0%
'I had sex with a porn star
during Shark Week' show?

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:33.039
I think I'd be a good guest.
Maury?"

00:09:33.039 --> 00:09:34.507
The big news that
came out of the town hall

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:37.476
was the president refusing to
disavow a conspiracy theory

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.611
he re-tweeted that
Barack Obama and Joe Biden

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:42.915
had the members of the
Osama bin Laden raid murdered

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:45.084
after they killed
a bin Laden body double

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:46.518
and not the actual bin Laden,

00:09:46.518 --> 00:09:49.087
who, according to this theory,
is still alive.

00:09:49.087 --> 00:09:50.489
Trump isn't qualified
to be president,

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:52.892
but he should definitely have
a 3:00 a.m. call-in show

00:09:52.892 --> 00:09:54.360
on public-access television.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.194
"Tonight's topic is
'Jurassic Park:

00:09:56.194 --> 00:09:59.899
A real place being covered up by
aliens working for the CIA?'

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:01.867
Can we put the number
up on the screen?

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:02.935
We can't?

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:04.936
Oh, because Kevin's
not here today?

00:10:04.936 --> 00:10:06.539
Okay. I forgot.

00:10:06.539 --> 00:10:09.141
Well, here's my first guest,
Curtis Sliwa."

00:10:09.141 --> 00:10:11.143 line:0%
Also, even if that
insane theory was true,

00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:13.045 line:0%
you sure that's the message
you want to close out

00:10:13.045 --> 00:10:14.179 line:0%
the election with?

00:10:14.179 --> 00:10:16.048
There might be an
out-of-control pandemic

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:17.516
and a once-in-a-century
economic crash,

00:10:17.516 --> 00:10:18.750
but don't worry, folks,

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:21.286
the world's most-wanted
terrorist is still alive.

00:10:21.286 --> 00:10:25.057
Do you guys remember Joe Biden's
famous line from 2012?

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:30.528
-Osama bin Laden is dead,
and General Motors is alive.

00:10:30.528 --> 00:10:31.997
-Well, a GM plant in Ohio

00:10:31.997 --> 00:10:35.100
closed after Trump
promised to save auto jobs.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.736
So I guess his new slogan is,

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:39.171
"GM is dead,
and Osama bin Laden is alive."

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:43.508
which, by the way,
was also a rejected "Ziggy."

00:10:43.508 --> 00:10:45.010
So, Hannity thought
it was an ambush.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.979
You might be asking,
"In what way exactly was

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.981
this town hall
biased against Trump?"

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:51.617
Well, on his radio show Monday,
Sean Hannity

00:10:51.617 --> 00:10:53.151
invited on a guest who broke

00:10:53.151 --> 00:10:56.355
maybe the biggest story yet
of the 2020 campaign.

00:11:36.561 --> 00:11:39.431
I wish that were true, only to
imagine how it went down.

00:11:39.431 --> 00:11:40.866
"Okay, I think we're almost
ready to go.

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:42.234
Let's just bring
those stools out.

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:46.605
Wait. That stool is too big.

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:50.608
Bring out the one
for only half a buttock."

00:11:50.608 --> 00:11:53.012
It's ridiculous that a chair for
Trump can be too small.

00:11:53.012 --> 00:11:54.747
I mean, even when
he has a giant chair,

00:11:54.747 --> 00:11:56.748
he only uses 6 inches of it.

00:11:56.748 --> 00:11:58.117
It doesn't matter
how big a chair is,

00:11:58.117 --> 00:11:59.317
he's going to sit like
he's watching

00:11:59.317 --> 00:12:00.819
the season finale of "24."

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:02.621
He's always lurching forward,

00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:04.589
like someone just slammed on
the brakes.

00:12:04.589 --> 00:12:05.825
When he meets
with world leaders,

00:12:05.825 --> 00:12:07.760
he should wear a seat belt.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.696
It's still just shocking to me
the degree to which grown adults

00:12:10.696 --> 00:12:11.864
on the right whine and moan

00:12:11.864 --> 00:12:13.331
about not getting special
treatment.

00:12:13.331 --> 00:12:15.934
Yesterday, for example,
Trump threatened to release

00:12:15.934 --> 00:12:19.572
footage from an interview
he agreed to do

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:21.807
with "60 Minutes"
correspondent Lesley Stahl,

00:12:21.807 --> 00:12:23.342
after angrily storming out.

00:12:23.342 --> 00:12:25.911
-Multiple sources telling CNN
now that President Trump

00:12:25.911 --> 00:12:30.549
abruptly ended a solo interview
with CBS's "60 Minutes" today.

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:32.784
And the president did not
return to the room

00:12:32.784 --> 00:12:35.987
for a joint interview with
Vice President Mike Pence.

00:12:35.987 --> 00:12:38.557
President Trump sat down with
CBS News' Lesley Stahl

00:12:38.557 --> 00:12:41.226
for 45 minutes
before getting up and leaving

00:12:41.226 --> 00:12:43.896
and telling CBS that he thought
they had enough material.

00:12:43.896 --> 00:12:46.532
-He also tweeted a 6-second
video clip of Stahl

00:12:46.532 --> 00:12:48.867
not wearing a mask while
talking with producers

00:12:48.867 --> 00:12:50.368
at The White House.

00:12:50.368 --> 00:12:52.905
The president later tweeted, "I
am pleased to inform you that,

00:12:52.905 --> 00:12:54.807
for the sake of
accuracy in reporting,

00:12:54.807 --> 00:12:56.641
I am considering posting
my interview

00:12:56.641 --> 00:12:59.845
with Lesley Stahl of
'60 Minutes' prior to airtime.

00:12:59.845 --> 00:13:01.580
This will be done
so that everyone

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:04.316
can get a glimpse of what
a fake and biased interview

00:13:04.316 --> 00:13:05.651
is all about."

00:13:05.651 --> 00:13:06.952
-Well, it sounds like
it went great.

00:13:06.952 --> 00:13:09.788
But it was at The White House,
so if the chair

00:13:09.788 --> 00:13:12.291
didn't have full-buttock
coverage, that's on you.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:14.359
I'd love to see the
Trump version of this interview.

00:13:14.359 --> 00:13:15.894
I'm guessing when
he releases the footage,

00:13:15.894 --> 00:13:17.295
it will look
something like this.

00:13:17.295 --> 00:13:19.531
-People are saying
you have so much money

00:13:19.531 --> 00:13:21.267
and you are going to win.

00:13:21.267 --> 00:13:24.703
-Oh, so, your big gotcha moment
is you caught Lesley Stahl

00:13:24.703 --> 00:13:26.105
not wearing a mask for what?

00:13:26.105 --> 00:13:27.439
Six seconds?

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:29.341
This will shock you,
but we have blockbuster footage

00:13:29.341 --> 00:13:32.277
of you not wearing a mask
at basically every public event

00:13:32.277 --> 00:13:33.511
you've ever done.

00:13:33.511 --> 00:13:35.981
Why does Trump think
this argument is a winner?

00:13:35.981 --> 00:13:37.482
Lesley Stahl
wasn't wearing a mask

00:13:37.482 --> 00:13:38.917
for 6 seconds
after an interview.

00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:41.287
Meanwhile, the day before he
tested positive for COVID,

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:44.056
Trump was tossing hats
into a packed crowd

00:13:44.056 --> 00:13:45.724
like the Phoenix Suns Gorilla.

00:13:45.724 --> 00:13:47.392
Hundreds of Americans
are dying every day,

00:13:47.392 --> 00:13:49.862
and the country is in the midst
of its third coronavirus wave,

00:13:49.862 --> 00:13:51.763
which is already nearing
new records

00:13:51.763 --> 00:13:53.965
and which experts predict
could be the worst yet,

00:13:53.965 --> 00:13:55.567
and amid all that,
The White House

00:13:55.567 --> 00:13:56.768
has decided to spend its time

00:13:56.768 --> 00:13:58.737
attacking a "60 Minutes"
correspondent,

00:13:58.737 --> 00:14:00.505
even going so far as
to spend time

00:14:00.505 --> 00:14:02.240
reviewing footage
of the interview,

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:05.010
searching for ways, I guess,
to make her look bad?

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.144
-He didn't walk out.

00:14:06.144 --> 00:14:08.380
I mean,
the characterization of that --

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:11.249
He spent over 45 minutes
with Lesley Stahl.

00:14:11.249 --> 00:14:12.817
I've looked at
every single minute

00:14:12.817 --> 00:14:14.886
of the interview and then some.

00:14:14.886 --> 00:14:16.588
-That's what you
were spending your time on?

00:14:16.588 --> 00:14:18.090
You're The White House
chief of staff,

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:20.192
not an intern for TV Guide.

00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:22.527
There's a raging,
out-of-control pandemic,

00:14:22.527 --> 00:14:23.796
and The White House
chief of staff

00:14:23.796 --> 00:14:25.798
is poring over tape of a
"60 Minutes" interview

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:28.433
like the Jets' defensive
coordinator after a blowout.

00:14:28.433 --> 00:14:29.668
"Okay, everybody.

00:14:29.668 --> 00:14:30.769
Do you guys see
what happened here?

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:33.672
We forgot. We forgot to what?

00:14:33.672 --> 00:14:36.342
We forgot -- Tackle.
Forgot to tackle.

00:14:36.342 --> 00:14:39.043
And what was --
What was he holding?

00:14:39.043 --> 00:14:41.613
The person we forgot to tackle.
Do you remember? No?

00:14:41.613 --> 00:14:43.682
It wasn't a pointy brown egg.

00:14:43.682 --> 00:14:46.051
Anybody? It was the football.

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:47.185
Okay, guys.

00:14:47.185 --> 00:14:49.154
Love to not go through this
every week."

00:14:49.154 --> 00:14:51.389
Trump and his toadies can whine
about the media all they want.

00:14:51.389 --> 00:14:54.092
It doesn't change the
basic story of the campaign.

00:14:54.092 --> 00:14:56.595
Nearly 300,000 more Americans
have died this year

00:14:56.595 --> 00:14:58.096
than otherwise would have,

00:14:58.096 --> 00:15:00.065
and 8 million
have gone into poverty,

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:01.232
and it could have been
prevented.

00:15:01.232 --> 00:15:03.468
Remember that when
Trump comes to your town,

00:15:03.468 --> 00:15:05.337
tells you he doesn't
want to be there, and says...

00:15:05.337 --> 00:15:06.705
-May I please have your vote?

00:15:06.705 --> 00:15:08.707
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:12.377
♪♪

00:15:12.377 --> 00:15:14.379
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:15:14.379 --> 00:15:17.016
over 2 million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:15:17.016 --> 00:15:19.784
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:15:19.784 --> 00:15:20.819
and they need your help.

00:15:20.819 --> 00:15:22.321
If you're watching this online,

00:15:22.321 --> 00:15:23.555
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:15:23.555 --> 00:15:26.091
Stay safe, wash your hands,
wear a mask.

00:15:26.091 --> 00:15:27.226
We love you.

